#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'TXT'
HOW TO ESCAPE THE WEIRDNESS
===========================
  Super+Shift+E     Earthling Mode: English labels, a normal dock, normal workspaces
                    (also a button inside the Mothership Eye, and offered at first boot)
  Ctrl+Alt+F3       a plain text console, always
  Boot menu         "LTS kernel, safe graphics" entry = known-good fallback
  Kernel param      zorp.earthling=1     forces Earthling Mode for that boot
  Kernel param      systemd.unit=multi-user.target   no graphics at all

Phase note: the Hive desktop arrives in a later build; this ISO is the TTY base.
TXT
